alex: Quick question — I'm landing a tiny Helm change in the service chart to wire the runtime token from a Secret, but I want it to be optional so we can roll this out without breaking existing installs. Current values snippet I have is:

alex: ```yaml
serviceToken:
  enabled: false
  secretName: my-service-token
  key: token
```

alex: and in the template I'm trying to do a safe lookup so pods don't get an env var with an empty string. My naive pattern was: 

alex: ```tpl
{{- $s := lookup "v1" "Secret" .Release.Namespace .Values.serviceToken.secretName }}
{{- if $s }}
- name: SERVICE_TOKEN
  valueFrom:
    secretKeyRef:
      name: {{ $.Values.serviceToken.secretName }}
      key: {{ $.Values.serviceToken.key }}
{{- end }}
```

alex: Does that look ok? Also there's a Terraform PR to start creating the ExternalSecret when `service_token = true` — worried about ordering if the k8s chart goes first. @morgan any thoughts on deploy ordering or a recommended pattern? :thinking_face:

morgan: That template is fine, but prefer guarding on the value flag too so the intent is explicit: `{{- if .Values.serviceToken.enabled }}` around the whole block. lookup is good if secret might be present but the flag controls rollout.

morgan: Regarding Terraform/ExternalSecret: we hit race conditions before where chart deploys before the ExternalSecret provider has synced, resulting in missing secrets for a short time. Two pragmatic options:
- Create the ExternalSecret as part of infra apply (earlier pipeline stage) so it's present before Helm.
- Keep chart optional and add an initContainer or preHook that retries on missing secret (ugly).

sasha: +1 to infra-first. If the ExternalSecret resource is created via Terraform, add a small manual `sleep`/`wait` step in the deploy pipeline that waits for `kubectl get secret my-service-token -n $NS` to succeed (or use `kubectl wait --for=condition=ready secret/...` if available). That keeps Helm simple. Also add a clear values doc entry so customers know `serviceToken.enabled` controls injection. :white_check_mark:

sasha: Also minor template nit: prefer using the `.Release.Namespace` for the lookup rather than a hardcoded namespace, and avoid double-dereferencing `$.Values` inside loops. Example: 

sasha: ```tpl
{{- if .Values.serviceToken.enabled }}
{{- $name := .Values.serviceToken.secretName }}
{{- if (lookup "v1" "Secret" .Release.Namespace $name) }}
- name: SERVICE_TOKEN
  valueFrom:
    secretKeyRef:
      name: {{ $name }}
      key: {{ .Values.serviceToken.key }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
```

deploy-bot: CI:terraform apply for infra/service-token-external created ExternalSecret/my-service-token in namespace production (run-id: 2873). :rocket:

alex: Great, I'll update the chart to gate on `enabled` and add the `lookup` check like Sasha's snippet. I'll also move the TF change to the infra stage so the ExternalSecret exists before Helm runs and add a pipeline wait (kubectl wait). I'll ping @morgan for code review when it's up. Thanks all :pray:
